"But", "s": 56.24, "e": 56.39, "c": ""}, {"w": "here's", "s": 56.39, "e": 56.7, "c": ""}, {"w": "the", "s": 56.7, "e": 56.85, "c": ""}, {"w": "part", "s": 56.85, "e": 57.06, "c": ""}, {"w": "that", "s": 57.06, "e": 57.26, "c": ""}, {"w": "surprises", "s": 57.26, "e": 57.72, "c": ""}, {"w": "people", "s": 57.72, "e": 58.08, "c": ""}, {"w": "The", "s": 58.08, "e": 58.23, "c": ""}, {"w": "government", "s": 58.23, "e": 58.75, "c": "red"}, {"w": "already", "s": 58.75, "e": 59.1, "c": ""}, {"w": "knew", "s": 59.1, "e": 59.36, "c": ""}, {"w": "Would", "s": 59.62, "e": 59.7, "c": ""}, {"w": "you", "s": 59.7, "e": 59.8, "c": ""}, {"w": "carry", "s": 59.8, "e": 60.02, "c": ""}, {"w": "a", "s": 60.02, "e": 60.16, "c": ""}, {"w": "million", "s": 60.16, "e": 60.38, "c": "red"}, {"w": "in", "s": 60.38, "e": 60.58, "c": ""}, {"w": "cash", "s": 60.58, "e": 60.8, "c": ""}, {"w": "Yes", "s": 61.18, "e": 61.26, "c": "grn"}, {"w": "or", "s": 61.26, "e": 61.44, "c": ""}, {"w": "no", "s": 61.44, "e": 61.66, "c": ""}], "lines": [{"i": 0, "text": "If you walk into a bank and ask for $1 million in cash, right now, will they hand it over?", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.34}, {"i": 1, "text": "Mike tries it. The teller opens his drawer. Not even close.", "start": 4.62, "end": 7.5}, {"i": 2, "text": "He checks the vault too. Still not enough.", "start": 7.78, "end": 9.75}, {"i": 3, "text": "His account says one million dollars. But the cash? It isn't in this building.", "start": 10.03, "end": 13.59}, {"i": 4, "text": "Most of the money in your account isn't paper at all. It's a number on a screen.", "start": 13.87, "end": 17.3}, {"i": 5, "text": "A branch only keeps the cash it expects to need. So the teller calls the manager.", "start": 17.58, "end": 21.37}, {"i": 6, "text": "Mike gets angry. It's his money. The manager just nods. You'll get it. Just not today.", "start": 21.65, "end": 25.75}, {"i": 7, "text": "Then he opens a form. For cash over ten thousand dollars, the bank reports it to the government.", "start": 26.03, "end": 30.43}, {"i": 8, "text": "Automatically. It's routine, not an accusation.", "start": 30.63, "end": 33.04}, {"i": 9, "text": "So where is the money? Banks order it from the Federal Reserve, and armored trucks carry it.", "start": 33.32, "end": 37.17}, {"i": 10, "text": "Mike leaves with nothing. Banks often ask for a day or two of notice.", "start": 37.45, "end": 40.7}, {"i": 11, "text": "Day one. Nothing. Day two. His phone rings.", "start": 40.98, "end": 43.05}, {"i": 12, "text": "Then the truck arrives. Ten thousand hundred-dollar bills. About twenty-two pounds.", "start": 43.35, "end": 47.17}, {"i": 13, "text": "A stack almost four feet tall. And it all fits in one backpack.", "start": 47.37, "end": 50.6}, {"i": 14, "text": "So did Mike get his million? Yes. After the wait.", "start": 50.88, "end": 53.32}, {"i": 15, "text": "He walks out with a backpack worth a million dollars.", "start": 53.52, "end": 55.96}, {"i": 16, "text": "But here's the part that surprises people. The government already knew.", "start": 56.24, "end": 59.36}, {"i": 17, "text": "Would you carry a million in cash? Yes or no?", "start": 59.64, "end": 61.81}]}